From 2545f90c3e4777e6d474cf78f570dda1a75ed050 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 01:50:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 099/294] pvr: hold clear-only dynamic render passes until a
 later pass uses the image

zink submits a pending glClear as its own render pass when the app switches
framebuffer: an empty pass that clears and stores a whole attachment, and
later a pass on the same image that loads it back. The empty pass costs
kernel jobs and a full tile store, and the load re-reads what it just wrote.

Do not submit a dynamic render pass that only clears (loadOp CLEAR, storeOp
STORE, render area equal to the whole view, no draws, no queries). Keep its
attachments as pending clears. A later pass that attaches the same image view
over the same area takes the clear as its own load op, if it still stores what
the clear would have stored (not STORE_OP_NONE or LOAD_OP_NONE). Anything else
that can see the image submits the clears first, at that point of the command
stream: a pass that attaches the image another way, secondary command buffers,
multiview or suspend/resume, a legacy render pass, a non-graphics sub-command,
a barrier that names the image or makes attachment writes visible to more than
fragment work, events, vkCmdExecuteCommands and vkEndCommandBuffer.

A draw that may read the image through a bound descriptor set (sets track the
images written into them, exactly up to 8, then any) makes the pass submit the
clear before itself: every sub-command the pass added is moved behind the
clear sub-commands. This also covers a pass that reads an image whose clear it
took over.

glmark2 off-screen (zink): desktop shadow 258 -> 286, desktop blur 209 -> 224,
shadow 242 -> 312 FPS, other scenes unchanged (full suite 641 -> 643). CTS
dr_list, rp_extra, caselist 1-3 and a 12000-case rendering sample give the
same results as before, glmark2 --validate 27/0. PVR_DEBUG=noclearfold turns
it off.
